{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Salman Humayun (Urdu: ‎ ) is a public policy expert with experience in managing, designing and delivering technical assistance and reform programs especially focusing on governance and education sectors in Pakistan.","title":"Salman Humayun"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He is currently the executive director at Institute of Social and Policy Sciences and the co-editor of Journal of Social and Policy Sciences.","title":"Salman Humayun"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" He is also member board of advisors at Centre for Public Policy and Governance, Forman Christian College, Pakistan.","title":"Salman Humayun"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Scott Christian College is a college in Nagercoil, Tamil Nadu.","title":"Scott Christian College"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was established in 1809.","title":"Scott Christian College"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It is one "A" College under NAAC ranking and is rated 5-star.","title":"Scott Christian College"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" It is also one of the nine colleges in Tamil nadu which were recognised by the central government as 'Institutes of Potential Research and Excellence' along with Madras University and Madurai Kamaraj University.","title":"Scott Christian College"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Scott Christian College is one of the earliest colleges in India along with Fort William College, Calcutta, started in 1800 which was closed in 1835, the Hindu College established in 1817 which was later named as Presidency University, Kolkata; the Serampore College in Serampore (Bengal) established in 1818 and the Bishop’s College, Calcutta(1820).","title":"Scott Christian College"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" It is the oldest college in the Erstwhile state of Travancore and Madras Presidency.","title":"Scott Christian College"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" Wikipedia says: "The Maharaja had occasion to visit a school that was imparting instruction in English at Nagarcoil under the auspices of the London Missionary Society (LMS).","title":"Scott Christian College"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" He was impressed by the school and the quality of the education given there and was convinced that the new type of school held out great prospects for the people of the state.","title":"Scott Christian College"},{"sentence_id":8,"text":" The school later evolved into Scott Christian College, Nagercoil.","title":"Scott Christian College"},{"sentence_id":9,"text":" Shortly thereafter he invited Mr. Roberts who was in-charge of the school at Nagarcoil to come to Thiruvananthapuram and start a similar school there.","title":"Scott Christian College"},{"sentence_id":10,"text":" The educationist, who was an Englishman, agreed and a new school was started in 1834."","title":"Scott Christian College"},{"sentence_id":11,"text":" The school started by Mr. Roberts has now blossomed into the University College, Thiruvananthapuram.","title":"Scott Christian College"},{"sentence_id":12,"text":" So Scott Christian College is also linked to University college, and both are now reputed colleges.","title":"Scott Christian College"},{"sentence_id":13,"text":" The alumni of the college are called Scottians.","title":"Scott Christian College"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Caliber International College is an institution of higher education at Rajbiraj, Nepal.","title":"Caliber International College"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The college is established in 2006.","title":"Caliber International College"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The founder of the college is Arun Yadav.","title":"Caliber International College"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The college belongs to the first group of colleges in Rajbiraj to receive academic accreditation from the Purbanchal University.","title":"Caliber International College"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The college offer 10+2 and Bachelor level courses.","title":"Caliber International College"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" This is the first college in Rajbiraj which offer Bachelor in Business Administration (BBA) stream under Purbanchal University.","title":"Caliber International College"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Kshitiz Educational Foundation is an institution of higher education at Tetari Gaachhi, Rajbiraj, Nepal.","title":"Kshitiz Educational Foundation"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The college is established in 2010.","title":"Kshitiz Educational Foundation"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The college belongs to the first group of colleges in Rajbiraj to receive academic accreditation from the Purbanchal University.","title":"Kshitiz Educational Foundation"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" At the beginning, the college offers only student of Bachelor in Business Administration (BBA) stream under Purbanchal University.","title":"Kshitiz Educational Foundation"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Later the college authority offer 10+2 level courses.","title":"Kshitiz Educational Foundation"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Forman Christian College is a independent research liberal arts university located in Lahore, Punjab, Pakistan founded in 1864.","title":"Forman Christian College"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The university is administered by the Presbyterian Church and follows an American-style curriculum.","title":"Forman Christian College"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Charles William Forman (1821–1894) was a Presbyterian minister, missionary and the founder of Forman Christian College, a private university in Lahore, Pakistan.","title":"Charles William Forman"}],"peer_messages":["":"Kshitiz Educational Foundation"}
